fix(codesign): give the exec'd process CS_PLATFORM_BINARY

A platform binary stayed a non-platform process, and launchd panicked with

    userspace panic: boot task is not a platform binary (mount-phase-1, /sbin/mount)

The trust-cache lookup hit and kebab_cs_classify_blob() did set
CS_PLATFORM_BINARY on the blob (kebab_cs_log_exec() prints platform=1),
load_code_signature() copied it into load_result.csflags, and
load_result.platform_binary marked the task (TFRO_PLATFORM).  The process
never got it: exec_mach_imgact() propagates load_result.csflags through a
fixed mask that has no CS_PLATFORM_BINARY, because on Apple platforms that
bit is AMFI's job.  p_csflags therefore never carried it, and
csops(CS_OPS_STATUS) -- which reports proc_getcsflags() -- told userland that
a platform binary was not one.

Derive the process bit from load_result.platform_binary, the same decision
that drives task_set_platform_binary(), so the process flag, the task flag
and the csops answer cannot disagree.  The policy gate is untouched:
kebab_cs_classify_blob() still decides whether a cdhash earns platform
status, and a blob it does not classify leaves the bit clear.

Update the comment in kebab_codesign.h that said the bit is never set by the
port.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -1410,6 +1410,26 @@
 		    CS_EXEC_SET_HARD | CS_EXEC_SET_KILL | CS_EXEC_SET_ENFORCEMENT);
 	} else {
 		imgp->ip_csflags &= ~CS_VALID;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * CS_PLATFORM_BINARY has no producer in xnu itself: AMFI sets it on the
+	 * blob when a trust cache classifies the cdhash as Apple platform code,
+	 * which is why it is deliberately absent from the csb_flags mask above.
+	 * This port replaces AMFI with kebab_cs_classify_blob(), and
+	 * load_result.platform_binary is that decision: it is the same field that
+	 * marks the task (task_set_platform_binary(), above) and the same one
+	 * kebab_cs_log_exec() prints as "platform=1".
+	 *
+	 * Without this the process's p_csflags never carries the bit, so
+	 * csops(CS_OPS_STATUS) -- which reports proc_getcsflags() -- tells
+	 * userland that a platform binary is not one, and launchd refuses to run
+	 * the boot task.  Propagating the decision does not widen the policy:
+	 * kebab_cs still decides, and a blob it does not classify leaves the bit
+	 * clear.
+	 */
+	if (load_result.platform_binary) {
+		imgp->ip_csflags |= CS_PLATFORM_BINARY;
 	}
 
 	if (proc_getcsflags(p) & CS_EXEC_SET_HARD) {
diff --git a/bsd/kern/kebab_codesign.h b/bsd/kern/kebab_codesign.h
--- a/bsd/kern/kebab_codesign.h
+++ b/bsd/kern/kebab_codesign.h
@@ -32,7 +32,9 @@
  *	Classify a code-signed binary as a platform binary when its cdhash is in
  *	Apple's static trust cache (the "StaticTrustCache" component of the
  *	IPSW).  Without this, nothing in the kernel can ever set
- *	CS_PLATFORM_BINARY, because that bit is set by AMFI.
+ *	CS_PLATFORM_BINARY, because that bit is set by AMFI.  With it the bit is
+ *	set on the blob here and propagated to the exec'd process by kern_exec.c,
+ *	which is what csops(CS_OPS_STATUS) and launchd's boot-task check read.
  *
  * KEBAB_CS_GRANT_ENTITLEMENTS
  *	Make the built-in AMFI provider answer entitlement queries with success
